  "_readme": "Named large employers a Benelux/EU search is expected to contain, as an operator-editable seed. This file deliberately holds NO ats_vendor and NO ats_slug: a guessed slug is a 404 that gets stored, re-probed and counted (docs/Data_Gathering_Plan.md section 6.7). Boards are resolved from each company's own careers page by scripts/resolve_employer_seed.py, which fetches through the egress layer (robots.txt honoured, FR-182) and confirms the slug with one request before storing it (detect_ats_verified, FR-222). Companies whose board does not resolve are still written to the company table: an employer with no readable board is exactly the case the speculative track (FR-262) exists for. Add your own rows freely - name and domain are the only required fields.",
  "why": "The board registry is built from public URL indexes and is therefore shaped like those indexes: Personio and Recruitee SMEs, Teamtailor's Nordic base, and the Greenhouse/Ashby boards that appear in Hacker News 'Who is hiring' threads. That is a startup and scale-up inventory. The large IT employers a Benelux search is judged on - the consultancies, the integrators, the telcos - run Workday, SuccessFactors or their own careers sites and appear in none of those indexes, so no campaign could ever surface them however long it ran.",
